## 5. WIT and Chern Rows Are Outputs

Once `V` exists, let

```text
Z = C_phys x_K3 X.
```

The inverse Poincare kernel and `L_alpha` have opposite twists. Their product
is therefore an ordinary line bundle `M` on `Z`. The projection

```text
f: Z -> X
```

is finite flat of degree three, so

```text
Psi(j_*L_alpha) = f_*M,
R^i f_*M = 0 for i>0,
rank(f_*M) = 3.
```

Thus WIT0 and local freeness are not a second search after `V`.

The same input has

```text
det(p_*O_C) = O_K3(-27H),
Nm(L_alpha) = O_K3(27H).
```

The determinant cancels. The graph-Prym and GRR rows then give

```text
c1(V3)=0,
c2(V3)=9u,
c3(V3)=+6 Omega.
```

The fifth and sixth literal rows remain physically unavailable until `V`
exists, but their implication theorems are closed. They are compiler outputs,
not independent source choices.

